{%- comment -%}
  CAVIERA — THREE WORLDS (Phase 1) — world-to-world transition foundation.

  Rendered once between each pair of adjacent worlds (Threshold→Constant, Constant→Editions,
  Editions→Commissions) — see sections/caviera-three-worlds.liquid. Purely a DOM/CSS foundation for
  a LATER phase's real transition (per brief Step 6): no wipe, no mask animation, no 3D morph exists
  yet. In Phase 1 this renders as a zero-height, non-visual hook only (see .caviera-world-transition
  in assets/caviera-three-worlds.css) — it cannot be seen and does not affect any world's layout or
  spacing; it exists purely so a later phase has an already-wired DOM location to build a real
  transition into without restructuring the section again.

  Params: from / to — the two data-world values either side of this transition, exposed as data
  attributes only (no logic reads them yet).
{%- endcomment -%}
<div
  class="caviera-world-transition"
  data-transition-from="{{ from }}"
  data-transition-to="{{ to }}"
  aria-hidden="true"
>
  <div class="caviera-world-transition__mask"></div>
  <div class="caviera-world-transition__surface"></div>
</div>
